Remaining issues:

1. Verse 1 (fly): the comment line ends with "\n", and after that, since animal == "fly", flyLine is not appended → a trailing newline remains, producing an extra blank line at the end. Fix: don't put a newline after the comment, or handle the fly case. The simplest is: write the comment without a trailing newline, and only add "\n" when there are subsequent lines. Alternatively, trim the trailing newline at the end.

2. Verse 8 (horse): the cumulative loop must not run for the horse. Fix: only loop when animal != "horse".

Let's restructure:

```go
func Verse(v int) string {
	var b strings.Builder
	animal := animals[v-1]
	fmt.Fprintf(&b, "I know an old lady who swallowed a %s.\n", animal)
	fmt.Fprintf(&b, "%s", comments[animal])
	if animal == "horse" {
		return b.String()
	}
	fmt.Fprintf(&b, "\n")
	for i := v - 2; i >= 0; i-- {
		suffix := ""
		if animals[i] == "spider" {
			suffix = " that wriggled and jiggled and tickled inside her"
		}
		fmt.Fprintf(&b, "She swallowed the %s to catch the %s%s.\n", animals[i+1], animals[i], suffix)
	}
	if animal != "fly" {
		fmt.Fprintf(&b, "%s", flyLine)
	}
	return b.String()
}
```

In the fly case: the comment is flyLine, then "\n", then no loop, and since animal == "fly" flyLine is not appended. Result: "I know ...\n" + flyLine + "\n" → trailing newline. Hmm, still a trailing newline.

Better approach: trim trailing newlines at the end: `return strings.TrimRight(b.String(), "\n")`. This handles all cases: fly (comment is the last line), horse, others (flyLine has no trailing newline).

